1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.869
As the final step, you will build a full stack coding agent

2
00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:06.573
that can edit multiple files and generate a complete web app.

3
00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:09.876
You will also learn how to manage long context efficiently

4
00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:12.779
with runtime summarization. Let's innovate.

5
00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:15.382
creating web apps is a complex task.

6
00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:18.985
It involves a lot of file editing, generating code, and many more.

7
00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:22.689
Thus, our agent will need tens of loops to complete it.

8
00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:26.593
This will inevitably fill up our context very quickly.

9
00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:29.896
We need a strategy to compress context at runtime

10
00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:32.966
while the user is interacting with the agent.

11
00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:36.169
To compress context, there are many strategies.

12
00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:38.772
We use a Runtime Summary.

13
00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:41.574
First, we need to define a fixed amount of tokens

14
00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:43.610
quantity in the context window at any time.

15
00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.612
For example, 40000 tokens.

16
00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:48.815
Then, we'll compress a percentage of the tokens.

17
00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:51.618
We will follow Gemini CLI in this case,

18
00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:54.120
which compresses 70% of the messages,

19
00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.822
starting from the oldest one,

20
00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:58.591
keeping last interactions unchanged.

21
00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:02.962
Then, we send the tokens to be summarized to a language model

22
00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:05.565
and inject back the summary into the context

23
00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:07.967
and replace the old messages.

24
00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:10.970
If our agent's context is full,

25
00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:15.375
we take 70% of the messages starting from the oldest.

26
00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:18.144
and compress them.

27
00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:21.147
Then we replace the old messages

28
00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:23.149
with the summary and continue.

29
00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.718
To compress the messages,

30
00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:28.421
we will use an LLM with a specific system prompt,

31
00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:31.324
designed for creating a snapshot of the conversation.

32
00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:35.528
Then, we craft a synthetic user message containing the snapshot

33
00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:38.031
and an assistant message to acknowledge it.

34
00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:40.934
These two messages are inserted into the context,

35
00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:44.938
substituting the initial ones. So, let's jump in.

36
00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:47.140
to the lab and put all of

37
00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.042
this into building a Full Stack Agent.

